    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144-a1">

                <pb facs="0690" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v04/pg665"/>


                <head>Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Brzezinski) to Secretary of Defense Brown<anchor n="4" xml:id="d144-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian">undated</date></dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>DOD’s Study of the US–USSR Military Investment Balance (S)</item>
                </list>
                <p>I have reviewed the subject paper you sent to the President on 5 July. Although
                    it’s an impressive piece of work and it presents an important message, the paper
                    may characterize the defense investment imbalance too unfavorably and even the
                    executive summary is much too long to ask the President to read. (S)</p>
                <p>Because the message of this study is very important and disturbing, I urge you to
                    prepare a short 3–5 page memo for the President that: <list>
                        <label>—</label>
                        <item>crisply summarizes the study;</item>
                        <label>—</label>
                        <item>states the appropriate caveats (our staffs have discussed the more
                            important ones); and</item>
                        <label>—</label>
                        <item>states your own view of the implications for our defense spending and
                            policies. (S)</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Zbigniew
                                Brzezinski</hi><anchor n="5" xml:id="d144-f2"
                    /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
